What is Automotive Plastics Recycling?
Automotive Plastics Recycling involves the systematic recovery and reprocessing of plastic components from end-of-life vehicles (ELVs) and manufacturing waste streams. The process focuses on materials like bumpers, dashboards, interior trims, and under-the-hood components typically made from polypropylene (PP), polyethylene (PE), and polyvinyl chloride (PVC). Through processes including sorting, cleaning, shredding, and reforming, these materials are transformed into reusable raw materials suitable for various automotive and non-automotive applications.
